# Fluxbridge — environment variables (all optional)
# Copy to .env or export these before launching. .env is git-ignored.

# --- Tradovate accounts ---
# There are NO Tradovate credentials here. Each login is token-only and is
# configured in the dashboard under Settings -> Tradovate Accounts (one access
# token per login). Tokens are auto-renewed via renewaccesstoken (access ->
# check token) and persisted in the SQLite database below.

# --- Data directory (persist the database / tokens across deploys) ---
# Holds fluxbridge.db (users, areas, settings, invites, audit log).
# NEVER point a v4 (main) and a v5 instance at the same directory at the same
# time: both would renew the same tokens and execute the same webhooks twice.
# NEXUSPRED_DATA_DIR=/var/data

# --- Dashboard login: user accounts (invite-only, multi-tenant) ---
# On first run, open the dashboard and create the first admin account at
# /setup; the admin invites additional users from Settings -> Users.
# Recommended: pin the session-cookie signing key so logins survive a move of
# the data directory (else it's auto-generated once and stored in the DB):
# SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# --- Server ---
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=9000
# Canonical public origin (custom domain). The dashboard then shows webhook
# URLs on this host no matter which hostname it was opened on, and emailed
# invite / password-reset links are built on it instead of the request's Host
# header. Strongly recommended on any public deployment.
# NEXUSPRED_PUBLIC_URL=https://bridge.hurenzone.ch

# --- Auto-updater branch (default: main) ---
# v5 lives on main. To pin an install to the previous line use backup/v4.11.0.
# NEXUSPRED_BRANCH=main

# --- Discord signal listener (optional module) ---
# Configured entirely in the dashboard (Settings -> Discord Listener): the user
# token, watched channel IDs, webhook targets and the dry-run switch are stored
# per area in the database, not here. Requires discord.py-self (in requirements.txt).
